OL,3,GNEWSAAsbestos killed my mum in her 40s
OL,4,A` was her school to blame?
OL,5,
OL,6,FWhen Caroline Bryan was enjoying high
OL,7,Fschool with friends in the early '90s,
OL,8,Fshe would never have imagined replaying
OL,9,Fthose memories in her final weeks,
OL,10,Fwhile searching for answers about her
OL,11,Fterminal condition.
OL,13,FThe mum was 46 when she died from
OL,14,Fmesothelioma, an incurable cancer
OL,15,Flinked to asbestos exposure.
OL,17,FAs she came to terms with her difficult
OL,18,Fdiagnosis, Caroline's belief was the
OL,19,Fonly place she could have encountered
OL,20,Fasbestos was during her time at school
OL,21,Fdecades earlier.
OL,23,APub: 24-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
